# AutoCAD leaves these beside a drawing the moment anyone opens one: a .bak of the previous
# save, a .dwg if it is saved in AutoCAD's own format, a lock file while it is open, a plot log,
# and Explorer's "- Copy" duplicates.  None of them is a deliverable, and the publish step copies
# dxf/ wholesale, so without this they would end up in the public repo beside the real drawings
# with no way for a reader to tell which is which.
*.bak
*.dwg
*.dwl
*.dwl2
*.sv$
*.ac$
plot.log
* - Copy.*
*.err

# The clip photographs are for sending to a manufacturer, not a deliverable on the drawing
# register, and the publish step copies whole directories.  Keeping them out of the repo is what
# keeps them off the website.
_clip_renders/
